            <ArticleTitle>[Anesthetic management using vasopressin for a patient complicated with septic shock].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1398-400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We reported anesthetic management of a patient complicated with septic shock. Catecolamines were not effective to improve severe hypotension. Therefore, vasopressin was used and this improved the severe hypotension. Vasopressin may be useful for a patient complicated with septic shock and severe hypotension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
